  <section class="section" id="faq">
    <div class="wrap faq">
      <div class="copy"><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:16px">Questions</p><h2 class="display" style="font-size:clamp(32px,3.8vw,48px)">Short answers.</h2><a class="btn btn-ghost" style="margin-top:24px" href="https://docs.openmesh.network" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Full spec in the docs →</a></div>
      <div>
        <details open><summary>What is a compute future?</summary><p>A contract for GPU-hours or node-months in a specific quarter at a price agreed today. Close early, or hold to delivery.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What backs a contract?</summary><p>Verified capacity only. No synthetic supply.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Cash or physical?</summary><p>Both. Cash closes at the final index; physical resolves into a redemption right on real infrastructure.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How do I start?</summary><p>Connect a Solana wallet — Phantom, Solflare or Backpack — deposit USDC, and trade any listed market. Infrastructure owners apply to list capacity from the Capacity Market.</p></details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
